1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,949
This is our T1, a ten-litre spray drone.

2
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:05,933
Six hundred thousand drones like it now work farms.

3
00:00:06,153 --> 00:00:08,469
Every one comes with an app that plans the flight.

4
00:00:08,689 --> 00:00:10,642
None of them plans the operator's day.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:15,700
In India, a Drone Didi gets eight or nine minutes of spraying per battery, then

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,148
waits two hours to charge.

7
00:00:17,368 --> 00:00:19,943
Jobs fly in booking order, into the noon wind.

8
00:00:20,163 --> 00:00:23,329
In one state, ninety percent of these operators lose money.

9
00:00:23,549 --> 00:00:24,931
The problem isn't the drone.

10
00:00:25,151 --> 00:00:25,874
It's the day.

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,176
FieldPilot is the missing layer.

12
00:00:28,396 --> 00:00:33,114
NVIDIA Nemotron, on Nebius Token Factory, reads the bookings, plans the day around

13
00:00:33,114 --> 00:00:37,486
the weather, the rules and her batteries, and hands the pilot a flight card.

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,426
Seven bookings, in any local language.

15
00:00:41,646 --> 00:00:46,376
Nemotron three point five Lightning turns them into schema-checked JSON, then code

16
00:00:46,376 --> 00:00:48,683
checks every number against the message.

17
00:00:48,903 --> 00:00:52,322
A local unit like the bigha gets flagged for a call, never guessed.

18
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:54,238
Plan my day.

19
00:00:54,458 --> 00:00:58,784
Green is when the rules allow spraying at each farm, and sorties are packed onto

20
00:00:58,784 --> 00:00:59,919
her two battery sets.

21
00:01:00,139 --> 00:01:04,657
The usual way flies five sorties outside the window, and wastes thirty-nine litres

22
00:01:04,657 --> 00:01:05,043
of mix.

23
00:01:05,263 --> 00:01:07,221
FieldPilot: none, and under two.

24
00:01:07,441 --> 00:01:11,509
Then Nemotron writes her brief in her own language, for under a tenth of a cent.

25
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:14,734
Drones now spray over two hundred million hectares a year.

26
00:01:14,954 --> 00:01:19,293
Count just a quarter of the gain we simulated, and FieldPilot saves about

27
00:01:19,293 --> 00:01:23,752
thirty-five million battery cycles, sixty-five million dollars, and seventy

28
00:01:23,752 --> 00:01:26,308
million litres of wasted spray, every year.

29
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:32,186
At the farm, Nemotron 3 Super runs the tools, and Super VL reads each zone's

30
00:01:32,186 --> 00:01:32,636
photos.

31
00:01:32,856 --> 00:01:37,778
A gate calibrated on a hundred and fifty labelled leaves passes healthy zones, and

32
00:01:37,778 --> 00:01:39,519
sends unsure ones to a human.

33
00:01:39,739 --> 00:01:40,648
She confirms.

34
00:01:40,868 --> 00:01:43,616
The crop twin says only one zone pays to spray.

35
00:01:43,836 --> 00:01:48,084
And with an eighty-six percent chance of rain, the safety checks refuse to fly.

36
00:01:48,304 --> 00:01:49,559
Nemotron proposes.

37
00:01:49,779 --> 00:01:50,787
Physics decides.

38
00:01:51,007 --> 00:01:52,054
A human approves.

39
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,639
This is the hardware it plans for.

40
00:01:54,859 --> 00:01:57,640
Our T1, on a JIYI K3-A Pro controller.

41
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:00,005
These are our own FieldPilot drone runs.

42
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,451
The controller is closed, so FieldPilot doesn't replace the pilot.

43
00:02:05,671 --> 00:02:10,319
It hands her a flight card: the zones, the line spacing, the speed, the dose, and

44
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,155
exactly how many litres to load.

45
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:19,243
To prove the cards fly, a twin of the K3-A Pro flies them, and runs the tank dry

46
00:02:19,243 --> 00:02:21,544
within four metres of the planned cut.

47
00:02:21,764 --> 00:02:26,545
On open firmware, unmodified ArduPilot flew our plan within one percent of its

48
00:02:26,545 --> 00:02:27,403
time and dose.

49
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,566
Asked alone, Nemotron would have flown in eleven of eighteen situations where it

50
00:02:33,566 --> 00:02:34,087
shouldn't.

51
00:02:34,307 --> 00:02:35,714
FieldPilot: zero.

52
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,411
Every battery, every litre, only where the crop needs it.

53
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:57,070
FieldPilot, by Future Agri.
